# TestFlight batch cuts — NON-NEGOTIABLE

Apple / ASC internal TestFlight slots are **scarce (~15 builds per month)**. Never burn a slot on one PR or one feature.

## When the user says push / cut TestFlight

1. Identify the **previous TestFlight ship commit** (last `1.3.0 (N)` cut documented in `docs/make-v*-testflight-notes.md` or the last EAS `testflight` build commit).
2. Fold **all product work since that cut** onto the current `cursor/make-v*` tip — every finished PR tip / commit that landed between the two pushes.
3. Build **one** IPA from that fold tip (`eas build --profile testflight --auto-submit`).
4. Record the cut in `docs/make-v*-testflight-notes.md` listing what was included.

## Forbidden

- Single-work TestFlight pushes (one bugfix, one feature branch, one agent task).
- Cutting TF from a narrow `cursor/*-c30d` tip while sibling Oct-day fixes sit unmerged.
- Opening a new EAS build “just to ship this one thing” when other finished work is waiting.

## Allowed exceptions (user must say so explicitly)

- Hotfix for a **production / store-blocking** crash where waiting to fold would strand testers.
- User names a **specific** subset (“TF only shared-device, skip the rest”).

Default when ambiguous: **fold everything since last TF**, then build once.
